Z||000008||MooCow||04-19-2001||03:35 PM||||I got this car from Ed Parks at the Fiero factory in January this year.  The engine was a 95 camaro engine with only 53,000 on it.  I have put about 1,000 on it before it died.  I know if it up and running again, but it now smokes.  My guess is that I clogged the cat because it would turn over but it never fired until I fixed a loose wire.  I kept trying to start it nearly every day for over two weeks hoping maybe it would start.  I know I should not have done that but I was hoping it would start on time.  Any suggestions??<P>                              Thanks Ken||||reg||1
Z||000009||Jake_Dragon||04-19-2001||05:23 PM||||Check your oil you could have loaded it up with fuel from trying to start the car.<BR>If it smells like gas than change it.<BR>If you have real thin oil it may help changing it and using something a little thicker.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||MooCow||04-19-2001||06:41 PM||||I did change the oil cause when i was moving the distrubutor to get the timming right I never tightend it down all the way and oil kept comming out.  I never knowticed till nearly all the oil was out.  So I gave it an oil change.  I also cleaned up all the oil that was on the engine block itself. I will find out if it is my cat next week when I get rodney's cat remover.<P>                              Thanks Ken||||reg||1
Z||000011||Indiana_resto_guy||04-19-2001||07:23 PM||||Ken,<P>Through the whole ordeal that you've just been through, it's possible that fuel and a small amount of oil escaped into the exhaust system.<BR>The system should clean itself out the more you drive it. Not a bad idea of removing the cat if it rattles. Was it new with the install of the 3.4?||||reg||1
